From 0c7295de0038d139a6fd828f3c0231fcf7890cb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:52:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Coordinate fusion: place graph nodes on the cognitive map

The try5 map path could not use map layout. The map encoder has no position
code, so its 100 spatial tokens are an unordered set (invariant to permuting
10x10 blocks), and graph nodes carry only egocentric position features, so
the graph->map cross-attention can match nodes to map tokens by content only.
On the historical LLM try5 policy a raster from another scene scores no lower
than the episode's own (65.96-66.01 vs 65.09, three donor seeds).

MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.coordinate_fusion (default False, try5 only) closes that:
  * every gmap entry gets its map-frame (row, col) in raster cells from its
    world position (node_pos / ghost_aug_pos, as in get_pos_fts), using the
    raster origin = episode start (x, z) - cached start_position, the frame
    the refiner's online evidence already uses;
    MAP_ENCODER.start_position_meters_per_unit gives the cache's unit
    (1.0 LLM / gt.legacy metres, 0.5 gt.online cells);
  * GraphMapCrossAttention adds a fixed per-head distance bias
    -c_h * |node - token centre|^2 (tokens, 5 m) to the attention logits:
    a third of the heads stay content-only, the rest use sigma = 2.5-20 m;
    STOP, padding and the metadata token get no bias;
  * EmbeddingGridMapEncoder adds a fixed 2D sin/cos code to the spatial
    tokens.
Buffers are non-persistent, so no parameters or state_dict keys are added and
checkpoints load with the flag on or off; with the flag off every code path
is unchanged. The residual projection stays zero-initialised, so at step 0
the fused output equals try5's. The fusion refuses to run without node
coordinates, and the trainer refuses the GT teacher with the flag on (the
teacher checkpoint was trained without it); the GRPO trainer does not pass
coordinates yet and fails fast. Pretraining is untouched.

scripts/distill/check_map_frame.py is the offline preflight: it maps each
episode's reference path into the raster with the trainer's transform and
reports how often it lands on a labelled region, also under the wrong unit
and with x/z swapped, so a GT cache must clearly prefer the configured unit.

Tests: flag adds no state; NaN coordinates reproduce try5 exactly; zero
residual is identity; per-batch/per-head bias matches a manual attention;
local heads peak on the token under the node; encoder is block-permutation
invariant without the code and not with it; the start maps to its cached
cell in both units.

